{#
    The rail: the mark, where you can go, and the things you configure.

    Fixed at 240px on anything wide enough for it and replaced by the bottom bar
    in `mobile_nav.twig` below 768px. Both draw the same lists, so the narrow
    screen loses the layout and none of the reach.

    What is not here: the design's Upgrade Plan card. Renovo is self-hosted and
    there is no plan to upgrade to, so the card would be an advertisement for
    something that does not exist. The space goes to the tools group, which is
    made of real destinations.
#}
<aside class="sidebar">
    <a class="sidebar-brand" href="/">
        <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 460 427" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <use href="#renovo-mark"></use>
        </svg>
        <span class="sidebar-brand-name">{{ instance_name }}</span>
    </a>

    <nav class="nav-group" aria-label="{{ t('nav.primary') }}">
        {% include 'partials/nav_links.twig' with {'links': nav.primary} only %}
    </nav>

    <nav class="nav-group sidebar-tools" aria-label="{{ t('nav.tools') }}">
        {% include 'partials/nav_links.twig' with {'links': nav.tools} only %}
    </nav>
</aside>
